  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Oromo vocal-and-instrumental tradition of central-southern Ethiopia and northern Kenya, the largest Cushitic-language-speaking community in the Horn of Africa. Repertoire spans geerarsa men's heroic chant, weedduu wedding songs, irreecha thanksgiving songs at Lake Hora Arsadi, and contemporary Afaan Oromoo political-protest song. Performance integrates voice-led melodic content with krar, masenqo, and kebero accompaniment. Modal vocabulary draws on qenet pentatonic with Borana-Macha-Tulama-Arsi regional cadential vocabulary.",
